From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 06:00:17 +0900
Subject: Select a Linux platform adapter with CLICKER_PLATFORM=linux

On Linux the adapter was always macos.py (tests/conftest.py stands in for the modules it imports).
With CLICKER_PLATFORM=linux, platform_adapter imports linux.py instead: this project's adapter for
KDE Plasma on Wayland (AT-SPI, KWin, portal), placed into the tree by the recipe's overlay. The tests
clear CLICKER_PLATFORM so the suite keeps its macOS stand-ins.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [the selection hook could go upstream with a Linux adapter; ours depends on rungic-cua]
X-Rungic-Tests: none (gap: the adapter is exercised by the voice agent's computer use, not by an acceptance scenario)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/64
---
 tests/conftest.py                         | 3 +++
 typesafe_computer_use/platform_adapter.py | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/conftest.py b/tests/conftest.py
index 6bfa8a7..a0d8400 100644
--- a/tests/conftest.py
+++ b/tests/conftest.py
@@ -44,6 +44,9 @@ def _stub(name: str) -> types.ModuleType:
     return module
 
 
+# The Linux adapter drives the desktop it runs on; it is chosen only on request, never in tests.
+os.environ.pop("CLICKER_PLATFORM", None)
+
 REAL_ACCESSIBILITY = not _absent("ApplicationServices")
 
 if _absent("Quartz"):
diff --git a/typesafe_computer_use/platform_adapter.py b/typesafe_computer_use/platform_adapter.py
index e8e8c7b..a57ecdb 100644
--- a/typesafe_computer_use/platform_adapter.py
+++ b/typesafe_computer_use/platform_adapter.py
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 """The desktop this process drives: one platform adapter, chosen once, behind one name.
 
 Every other module reaches the platform through `desktop` and never imports macos.py or windows.py
-itself. Windows gets windows.py. Every other OS gets macos.py, the default: on macOS it is the real
+itself. Windows gets windows.py. Linux gets linux.py when CLICKER_PLATFORM=linux
+(the Moto phone's Plasma desktop, set by its moto-clicker launcher). Every other OS gets macos.py, the default: on macOS it is the real
 adapter, and on the Linux test runner tests/conftest.py stands in for the modules it imports, so the
 suite runs there unchanged. Only the Windows path imports a Windows-only package.
 
@@ -11,6 +12,7 @@ them to it, parameter for parameter.
 
 from __future__ import annotations
 
+import os
 import sys
 from pathlib import Path
 from typing import Protocol
@@ -61,6 +63,8 @@ class Desktop(Protocol):
 
 if sys.platform == "win32":
     from . import windows as _adapter
+elif sys.platform == "linux" and os.environ.get("CLICKER_PLATFORM") == "linux":
+    from . import linux as _adapter  # the Moto phone's Plasma desktop, through moto-cua (docs/64)
 else:
     from . import macos as _adapter
 
